# FACTORY (the author, 2026-10-05): `@: h f(a)` receives a factory's result; this row wrote `h: f a` until then.
# Item 739: a held callable's result has the header's number type at the root -- size_t, unsigned,
# ulong and char through one adapter and caller-owned declared-width destinations.
# s(1) = 2^32 + 1, u(4000000000) = 4000000005, l(1) = 6;
# c('a') = 200 (the captured byte, above 127) and c('b') = 'b'.  Mutants: every held call through
# an int-width destination loses wide values; sharing CHAR result storage loses d after e.
# Entry 7.
fn: makeS (size_t: n) fn: (size_t: x) size_t
    fn: addS (size_t: x) size_t
        return: x + n
    return: addS

fn: makeU (unsigned: n) fn: (unsigned: x) unsigned
    fn: addU (unsigned: x) unsigned
        return: x + n
    return: addU

fn: makeL (ulong: n) fn: (ulong: x) ulong
    fn: addL (ulong: x) ulong
        return: x + n
    return: addL

fn: makeC (char: n) fn: (char: x) char
    fn: pickC (char: x) char
        if: x = 'a'
            return: n
        return: x
    return: pickC

@: s5 makeS(4294967296U)
@: u5 makeU(5U)
@: l5 makeL(5U)
char: expectedChar (cast: (char) 200)
@: pc makeC(expectedChar)
size_t: a (s5: 1U)
unsigned: b (u5: 4000000000U)
ulong: c (l5: 1U)
char: d (pc: 'a')
char: e (pc: 'b')
int: ok 0
if: a = 4294967297U && b = 4000000005U && c = 6U && d = expectedChar && e = 'b'
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
